      "content": "6.1 Demographic Profile"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Jammu & Kashmir has a literacy rate of 67.16% as per the 2011 Census, with male literacy at 76.75% and female literacy at 56.43%.",
        "Major higher education centers include University of Kashmir (est. 1948), University of Jammu (est. 1969), NIT Srinagar, IIT Jammu, and IIM Jammu.",
        "Renowned GI Tags from the region include Kashmir Saffron, Pashmina, Kani Shawl, Sozani Craft, Paper Mache, Walnut Wood Carving, and Khatamband.",
        "CSIR-Indian Institute of Integrative Medicine (IIIM) in Jammu is a leading research center for drug discovery and aromatic plant studies.",
        "Pampore is globally recognized as the 'Saffron Town of Kashmir' for its extensive high-quality saffron cultivation."
      ],
      "id": "m8x6jsi"
    },
